## Decisions already made — please don't reverse these without asking

**Standing rules**

- Nothing bypasses `scrub()` — no bulk action, callback, manual dial, redial or phone feature.
- Re-pooling leads grants extra attempts, never resets `attempts_count`.
- Whoever owns a call is the only one who can edit it; everyone else, including admins, is view-only.
- Nobody verifies and closes the same customer, except by an audit-logged admin override.
- Admins have everything; restrictions apply to verifiers and licensed agents, controlled from the Permissions grid and per-user overrides.
- Rates are never computed from tiny samples; users are compared to the team median, never ranked.
- The app never shows a figure it can't verify; estimates are labelled as estimates.
- Depth over coverage on compliance work.
- Every prompt ends with: test in the real browser and reconcile on-screen numbers against the database.
- Claude Code can't reach the server laptop, my phone, or the Twilio and Retell dashboards: anything there is MANUAL TEST REQUIRED, never claimed as passing.

**Added since the last handoff**

- Lead cost always uses the price stamped when the leads were bought.
- Every lead source is people-only until I record a consent wording version that covers AI calls and clear that source. One clearance per source, not per call.
- Full bank routing/account numbers are visible only to admins: in the Carrier submissions download and admin receipts. Agents see no bank data at all. One audit log for bank data.
- External sales are recorded but never become our policies. An external sale waits for admin confirmation; nobody confirms their own.
